  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "In his previous life Fang Yuan had wanted an Immortal Gu House for exploring the River of Time and letting subordinates join rank eight battles, but those attempts stayed incomplete or weak. In this life he conceptualizes a time path Immortal Gu House under that revised plan.",
      "chapters": [
        1794
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "sys_immortal_gu_house",
        "loc_river_of_time",
        "path_time"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Deviation (recorded): this page is filed under gu-houses because Myriad Year Flying Warship is a named Immortal Gu House. It is mobile, not a five-region map seat.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "When construction finishes, the house reveals itself as a rank eight Immortal Gu House. Its core is Years Flow Like Water, and that core is what elevates the house to rank eight. Fang Yuan’s first creation is directly a rank eight Immortal Gu House. Main supplementary Immortal Gu are rank seven Precaution, used to raise defense after his older divination tortoise transformation no longer fits him, and rank seven Fight, a rule path Gu that coordinates with Years Flow Like Water. The warship has a narrow small-boat structure, shines with dazzling silver light, and gives a strong feeling of sharpness and toughness. Heavenly Court had failed to construct Eternal Yacht; Fang Yuan succeeds here through time path quasi-supreme grandmaster attainment plus rule path great grandmaster and formation path grandmaster levels.",
      "chapters": [
        1795
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "construction-and-core",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_years_flow_like_water",
        "sys_immortal_gu",
        "gu_precaution_immortal_gu",
        "gu_fight_immortal_gu",
        "fac_heavenly_court",
        "house_eternal_yacht"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Inside Mini Red Heaven, an immemorial year pig rushes out of a silver-lit formation. The immortals control Myriad Year Flying Warship and battle that immemorial year pig; both sides are evenly matched until the beast loses after days of fighting. Fang Yuan uses the fights to familiarize his rank seven subordinates with the house for later rank eight battles, and to gather immemorial year beasts toward a Twelve Zodiac battle formation plan.",
      "chapters": [
        1803
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "aperture-combat-training",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_mini_red_heaven",
        "move_twelve_zodiac_battle_formation"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Immortal Gu House Myriad Year Flying Warship moves in the River of Time with Fang Yuan on the bow. Present and Past Pavilion detects it at once and sends river waves, then a sawtooth whirlpool that immobilizes ordinary targets. The warship stays intact under that sawing assault, then turns surrounding water into expanding silver-white rapids and charges through. Its speed shocks the Four Xunzi controlling Present and Past Pavilion.",
      "chapters": [
        1805
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "river-of-time-clash",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "house_present_and_past_pavilion",
        "char_shang_xunzi"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Against Heavenly Court’s Gu Liu Ru, subordinates suggest torrential charge, which can change surrounding River of Time flow and drive the warship at astonishing speed; Fang Yuan instead orders daybreak sword. Myriad Year Flying Warship fires blinding white light that pulls river water into sharp silver blades, a rank eight time path killer move further amplified by the river. After breaking out of a later ambush, Fang Yuan names another house move, myriad year hunting, which draws a tide of year beasts, including ancient and immemorial year beasts, toward the field. Li Huang and Gu Liu Ru judge the house’s defense worthy of rank eight level when their attacks fail to stop it.",
      "chapters": [
        1811
      ],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "named-house-methods",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_gu_liu_ru",
        "char_li_huang"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "After Dragon Palace shatters, Fang Yuan and Wu Shuai enter Myriad Year Flying Warship, which is significantly faster than Dragon Palace and pulls away. Observers note that even though the warship is fast, its defense is inferior to Dragon Palace’s. Under continued pursuit it accumulates damage, dives underground, and finally disintegrates in black smoke. As with Dragon Palace earlier, they take back the core Immortal Gu with all their effort at the end before the warship breaks apart entirely.",
      "chapters": [
        2046
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "pursuit-and-destruction",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "house_dragon_palace",
        "char_wu_shuai"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan later says Myriad Year Flying Warship and Dragon Palace are destroyed, and that even if they still existed they would only be at peak rank eight level. The two rank eight Immortal Gu Houses were destroyed: Dragon Palace’s core Dream Token and Myriad Year Flying Warship’s Years Flow Like Water were preserved but injured and needed recuperation, while many other Immortal Gu, including Precaution and Fight, were destroyed in the battle.",
      "chapters": [
        2066
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "surviving-cores",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_dream_token"
      ]
    }
  ],
